// A separator after the last digit (LIT001, PROP-021 slice 21D). The number patterns
// (stdlib/core/lex/numbers.pilot) allow a `_` only between two digits, so
// `1000_` is not one number. Expected, worked by hand: its longest number is
// `1000`, and `_` follows it.
fn main() {
    print(1000_);
}
